JS

Provide interactive functionality for the website (e.g., toggles, animations, form handling).

Enhance user experience without affecting backend logic.

Can include vanilla JS or imported libraries, but should remain focused and modular

-----------------------------
Structure

- Each file should handle a specific feature or module (e.g., toggle.js, formValidation.js).
- Files are included in HTML templates via <script> tags or build tools.
- No server-side or database logic should be included.